<%#
  T-28 — the page a share link answers with when it will not serve.

  --- WHY THIS PAGE IS DELIBERATELY BARE ---

  Its reader is very often NOT a Redmine user: a public link (FR-62) is opened by whoever
  was sent it, on an instance they have no account on and whose navigation means nothing to
  them. So there is one sentence, and it is the whole page. No project, no template name, no
  "who to ask" — every one of those would tell a stranger something about an installation
  they have no relationship with, and the refusal is not made more useful by any of them.

  --- WHY IT LOOKS LIKE CORE'S OWN ERROR PAGE ---

  `h2` plus `p#errorExplanation` is exactly `app/views/common/error.html.erb`, which is what
  a Redmine 404 and 403 already look like — §9b's rule is native chrome, and a page that
  looks like the rest of the instance is what tells a reader the link reached the right
  place and simply is not live any more.

  NO ICON HELPER, and that is a version decision rather than an omission: core's error page
  calls `notice_icon`, which exists on Redmine 6+ and raises on 5.1 (D-3, the same divergence
  `reporter_dashboard_icon` shims). This controller declares no helper, and an anonymous
  error page is the last surface that should carry a version-specific call.

  NO "back" LINK either, though core's error page has one. `history.back()` from a link
  opened out of a mail goes nowhere, and to a stranger it offers to navigate into an
  instance they have no account on.
%>
<h2><%= l(:label_reporter_share_refused) %></h2>

<p id="errorExplanation"><%= @message %></p>

<% html_title l(:label_reporter_share_refused) %>
